 ## Unreleased
 
+### Added
+
+- `run --dataset review_low`: oliveyoung reads one board's low-rated reviews to
+  the end. The `suncare` board's top 10 products each get up to six
+  `RATING_ASC` pages of 50 -- every one-star review, then every two-star, the
+  cursor walk stopping early where the site runs out -- plus one `RATING_DESC`
+  page as a satisfaction baseline and the stats request for the site's own
+  rating distribution. 81 requests a run against the budget of 100. Same
+  `review` and `review_stats` tables as the `review` walk; what differs is
+  which products and how deep, which `scope` records under `review_low`.
+  Recommended cadence is daily: the site has no newest-first sort, and a daily
+  re-walk of the low end is what picks up new complaints. The `review` walk
+  itself is unchanged.
+
